Chapter: UnionFind
  cites Foreword chapter ListUtils

 Disjoint-set (union-find) with path compression and union by rank.
 O(alpha(n)) amortized per find and union operation. Essential for
 Kruskal MST, connected-component labeling, and equivalence classes.

 A UnionFind is a record containing:
   parent -- list mapping each element to its parent (self = root).
   rank   -- list of tree-depth upper bounds per root.
   count  -- number of disjoint components.

 A UfFindResult is a record containing:
   root -- the representative element of the component.
   uf   -- the union-find after path compression.

 To uf-new gives UnionFind,
   creating a union-find with the given number of singleton components.

 To uf-find gives UfFindResult,
   finding the root of the component containing the given element, compressing the path.

 To uf-union gives UnionFind,
   merging the components of two elements by rank; returns unchanged if already connected.

 To uf-connected gives Boolean,
   True if two elements belong to the same component.

 To uf-num-components gives Integer,
   returning the current number of disjoint components.

 We say:

Section: Type
  UnionFind = record {
    parent : List Integer,
    rank : List Integer,
    count : Integer
  }

Section: Construction
  uf-new : Integer -> UnionFind
  uf-new (n) = UnionFind { parent = uf-iota n 0 [], rank = list-zeros n, count = n }

  uf-iota : Integer, Integer, List Integer -> List Integer
  uf-iota (n) (i) (acc) =
    if i >= n then acc
    else uf-iota n (i + 1) (list-push acc i)

Section: Find with Path Compression
  UfFindResult = record {
    root : Integer,
    uf : UnionFind
  }

  uf-find : UnionFind, Integer -> UfFindResult
  uf-find (u) (x) =
    let p = list-at (u.parent) x
    in if p == x then UfFindResult { root = x, uf = u }
    else let result = uf-find u p
    in let compressed = UnionFind { parent = list-set-at (result.uf.parent) x (result.root), rank = result.uf.rank, count = result.uf.count }
    in UfFindResult { root = result.root, uf = compressed }

Section: Union by Rank
  uf-union : UnionFind, Integer, Integer -> UnionFind
  uf-union (u) (a) (b) =
    let fa = uf-find u a
    in let fb = uf-find (fa.uf) b
    in if fa.root == fb.root then fb.uf
    else let ra = list-at (fb.uf.rank) (fa.root)
    in let rb = list-at (fb.uf.rank) (fb.root)
    in if ra < rb then UnionFind { parent = list-set-at (fb.uf.parent) (fa.root) (fb.root), rank = fb.uf.rank, count = fb.uf.count - 1 }
    else if ra > rb then UnionFind { parent = list-set-at (fb.uf.parent) (fb.root) (fa.root), rank = fb.uf.rank, count = fb.uf.count - 1 }
    else UnionFind { parent = list-set-at (fb.uf.parent) (fb.root) (fa.root), rank = list-set-at (fb.uf.rank) (fa.root) (ra + 1), count = fb.uf.count - 1 }

Section: Queries
  uf-connected : UnionFind, Integer, Integer -> Boolean
  uf-connected (u) (a) (b) =
    let fa = uf-find u a
    in let fb = uf-find (fa.uf) b
    in fa.root == fb.root

  uf-num-components : UnionFind -> Integer
  uf-num-components (u) = u.count

